findings.body:
In `organize_agent_history`, the `ToolPromptMessage` content now comes from `tool_inputs`, when it used to come from `tool_responses`:

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="500-506"}

The code still computes `tool_responses` a few lines above, but nothing uses it anymore. On every later turn of an agent conversation, each past tool result in the prompt is replaced by the stringified arguments the tool was called with. For example, the model sees `{'query': 'weather'}` where `Sunny, 22°C` should be. The agent loses all earlier tool output, which breaks multi-turn agent chats in a way that's easy to miss. Wrapping the value in `str()` also turns dicts into Python repr instead of JSON.

::callout{type="warning"}
This isn't a typing change. It changes what the LLM sees, and no test in this PR covers `organize_agent_history`.

::suggestion{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="502-502"}
                                    content=tool_responses.get(tool, agent_thought.observation),

If the type checker complains about `content`, convert non-string values with `json.dumps`, not `str()`, and keep reading from `tool_responses`.

A new Pydantic model is added, but nothing in the codebase references it. `grep AgentThoughtValidation` only finds the definition.

::diff{file="api/core/agent/base_agent_runner.py" lines="52-65"}

It uses the old Pydantic v1 `class Config` style, which is deprecated in v2. The rest of the codebase uses `model_config = ConfigDict(...)`, for example in `core/rag/extractor/entity/extract_setting.py`. The inline comment also says the setting should be `extra='forbid'`, yet the code sets `allow`. Dead code whose own comment flags it as wrong will confuse future readers, and it also adds the `pydantic` import to this module. Delete it, or wire it into `create_agent_thought`/`save_agent_thought` with `model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid")`.
